{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/962506-splitting-the-party-yes-wanting-only-half-of-characters","id":962506,"title":"Splitting the Party - Yes, wanting only half of characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-02T14:39:57-07:00","id":962506,"title":"Splitting the Party - Yes, wanting only half of characters","content":"My <b>Mage </b>players PCs ventured into <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/925037-2e-ephemeral-beings-too-low-corpus?p=960214#post960214\">Astral Abyssal Realm of Carcosa to confront Hastur himself</a>. But they bring with them 4 NPCs and 1 player cannot be with us on session. So any ideas how to <i>split </i>party?<br /> <br /> Yes, I'm aiming to <i>divide</i> the team. I know roleplayers instincts are to stick to party. Yes, I know they would want to try anything to stay together. But I need ways to <i>split</i> them.<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure 'Suddenly, appears wall separating team' will work. I looked for articles on D&amp;D matter, but all are over how you should not split groups - or that small personal story lines are okay. Nothing on idea to split group <i>on purpose</i> by GM/ST.<br /> <br /> <b>How to make sure you will only have one half of team with you?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-03-2016, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T14:43:52-07:00","id":962508,"title":"","content":"Your group seems to be goal oriented, so present them with goals that can be best and most efficiently achieved by splitting up. Or, alternatively, can be achieved <i>only </i>by splitting up; for example, two things need to be deactivated or destroyed precisely at the same time, and they are in two different subrealms of the realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T19:46:09-07:00","id":962648,"title":"","content":"Goals that have to be achieved within less time than it would take to do them one after another definitely works, even if they're not things that have to be done precisely at the same time. You see this all the time in books and movies, the classic scenario is that of multiple bombs placed in different parts of a city and the only way to disarm them all in time is for the protagonists to split up. In your situation, perhaps Hastur is too strong to confront directly unless an object is destroyed, but if the group tries to destroy it before confronting Hastur, Hastur will simply arrive to stop them. So the only choice is to split up, with one group going to confront and distract Hastur while the other destroys the object, allowing the first group to then finish the job.<br /> <br /> Even if there's only one goal, if there's a time limit on getting it done, even presenting branching paths can result in the party splitting up. For example, the group is underground and the tunnel forks unexpectedly. The fork isn't on the maps they've been using, and there's no way to know which is the correct path. If they choose the wrong path and it doesn't lead where they need to be, they won't have enough time to backtrack, so the best option is to split up. (Little do they know that even those who take the &quot;wrong&quot; path will end up doing things that contribute to the success or failure of the mission.) Of course, in a Mage game this would be more difficult to pull off, since there are so many ways a Mage could determine which is the correct path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T18:10:34-07:00","id":963023,"title":"","content":"I state again: how amenable are the players and character to taking a deal, or running certain scenes separately? Because if you can sow seeds of doubt and suspicion, that will make other scenes or fights more interesting. And those are easiest when each character is out of earshot of the others. Who are they in the dark, and all that.<br /> <br /> As for how to split them? They are entering the Astral domain of an Abyssal lord of madness. Just relocate them as soon as someone loses direct contact with them. If you want to be really evil, <i>don't let them know that</i>, and have everyone else replaced by Abyssal and/or hallucinatory copies until the sudden but inevitable betrayal occurs, or they figure it out.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, have you selected the soundtrack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T21:53:59-07:00","id":963095,"title":"","content":"Runned game session - Could not split party how much I can, as Mastigos with Adept in Mind and Space cast Silver Threads from <b>Astral Realms </b>book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But then, using it costs Mana, so I made a hell sure they will few instances where they need to work for it. Game was also needed to be faster, as my partner was feeling sick.<br /> <br /> Still, next lesson learned - You cannot split party with high ranking Mastigos. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T22:22:18-07:00","id":963106,"title":"","content":"I do not comprehend how either the opening post or the latest ones are problems.<br /> <br /> And actually, you totes can split hte party with a high-ranking Mastigos. I have had it done to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T00:33:28-07:00","id":963118,"title":"","content":"It's an Abyssal Verge. There are loads of reasons that magic might mess up. Like, the King in Yellow already acts as a crowd of sleepers for paradox, why not give Carcosa dissonance? That silver thread isn't going to last long. Or, have the KiY use Influence Madness 5 on the Adept to make them dismiss their own spell (once people are seperated). Or just do what Vent0 suggested and ignore the rules. Carcosa twists the spells in arbitrary ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T00:51:20-07:00","id":963122,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a>, sure, in Abyssal Verge it could work, as it by definition breaks rules. In normal Astral - not so much, Mastigos is binding everyone.<br /> <br /> More, Adept of Space in material reality also makes party impossible to split - he just will teleport subject. Only problem it can be made if there are Sleepers in vicinity, but even then, Paradox is probably manageable thing still, with Mana most mages have with them.<br /> <br /> I'm slowly planning some Temples of Times Before for future sessions and I see that with Mastigos, whole party will always be with them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T04:06:11-07:00","id":963155,"title":"","content":"Random idea: Are there (or <i>weren't there</i> in Time Before ruins) parasites that might feed upon sympathetic connections themselves? Especially magically charged ones?<br /> <br /> Perhaps this line of though bears further investigation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T05:56:03-07:00","id":963182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/962506-splitting-the-party-yes-wanting-only-half-of-characters?p=963122#post963122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a><br /> I'm slowly planning some Temples of Times Before for future sessions and I see that with Mastigos, whole party will always be with them...</div> </div> </div> </div>Split timeframes maybe? Half the party &quot;freezes&quot;, the rest zip around in bullet time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T09:24:42-07:00","id":963248,"title":"","content":"Make them NOT WANT to stick together ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}